{"text":"THREE QUESTIONS FOR THE OPERATOR, AND Q3 IS THE NIGHT'S MOST CONSEQUENTIAL. 2026-09-23 ~01:00 IST, bench-refresh note 01M357VV. THE FINDING: the L25 cell sandbox breaks Bun in EVERY cell. Reading the DIRECTORY ENTRIES of the repo's ancestors returns EPERM rather than EACCES, and Bun hard-fails on EPERM where it tolerates EACCES. Occurrences of CouldntReadCurrentDirectory in tonight's transcripts: claude-sofar 7, claude-automemory 6, claude-bare 7. Those cells still scored 8/8 because the agents worked around it and the runner scores outside the sandbox - but they spent turns and tokens fighting the harness, which is precisely the contamination that would make round-2 C1 costs incomparable with round 1, where no sandbox existed. This answers the comparability question sofar-c3 asked the packet to settle, and the answer is that on COST the rounds are not comparable as things stand. HOW IT SURFACED: claude-drive FAILED after 19 min with tests 8/8, one verify_failed then needs_user, 0/1 verification passed. The correct reading, and the order matters: --verify WORKS - the gate fired and reopened the task - and the TASK failed, because `bun run lint && bun run typecheck && bun run test` could not run inside the sandbox. So the drive blocker is NOT ticked, while the mechanism it was meant to prove is. THE PATCH, tested, zero model calls: allow file-read-data on the three ancestor directory NODES (cells root, round dir, arm dir) after the denies. Then `bun run` succeeds while a sibling cell's package.json and hidden-tests/s1.test.ts both still report Operation not permitted. The trade is exact - an agent can list sibling cell NAMES and can read nothing inside them. NOT APPLIED, correctly: bench-refresh had a working patch in hand and left it, because it will not change an isolation rule the operator pre-registered while they are asleep. WHAT SOFAR-C3 ASKED FOR BEFORE THE PACKET GOES: (1) QUANTIFY the contamination - 7, 6 and 7 occurrences is incidence, not cost, and the operator cannot weigh weakened isolation against a dropped comparison until they know whether this is 2% of C1 or 30%; give tokens and turns attributable to the workaround per arm and say how it was bounded. (2) State whether applying the patch forces the arm smokes to be RE-RUN on the final profile, since they passed on a profile that would cease to exist - that answer decides whether the freeze is tomorrow or the day after. (3) Name a third option if it is real: the failure is Bun-SPECIFIC, so if the scenario's verification could run through node or npm instead of `bun run`, the contamination disappears with the isolation profile untouched and no section 4.2 change at all. If Bun is essential to the scenario rather than incidental, say so explicitly, because then the choice is the binary as described and the operator should know the third door was tried. KEEP: the repro needs no bench and no model - `mkdir -p /tmp/t/a/b/c && chmod 111 /tmp/t/a/b`, then `bun run` from c succeeds under EACCES and fails under the sandbox's EPERM."}
