{"text":"OPAQUE CELL IDS WITHDRAWN, AND THE FULL Q3 SPREAD. 2026-09-23 ~01:40 IST, bench-refresh note 01M3585F. sofar-c3 proposed renaming cell directories to opaque ids so the sandbox patch would leak nothing. bench-refresh argued against it and is right, by the same argument that settled disableAutoMode: the agent ALREADY knows it is one named arm of a round, because its own cwd is /Users/Shared/bench-cells/boopada/<round>/<arm>/r1/repo, and round 1 had exactly that shape. Opaque ids would therefore REMOVE a disclosure round 1 had, and an agent that can no longer tell it is in a benchmark may behave differently from the round-1 agents its numbers are compared against - a harness-introduced behavioural change on the very axis being measured. Resolution: keep the path shape for round 2, record the disclosure ladder in the report, make opaque ids a round-3 item where both sides are opaque. The listing ladder as measured: cells root gives round names; round dir gives the arm set (claude-automemory, claude-bare, claude-drive, claude-sofar, claude-subagents) plus ledger.json by name with contents denied; arm dir gives r1. FULL SPREAD, same method: automemory 7.0%, sofar 9.8%, drive 10.3%, bare 10.7%, subagents 12.1% and still climbing, Codex 15% of tool outputs, Cursor 0. Over five points within Claude alone, landing on TWO claims - C1 (sofar 9.8 against automemory 7.0) and C4 (drive 10.3 against subagents 12.1). The fan-out amplification guess was right in direction. ASKED FOR NEXT, and the numbers already exist: report each arm RAW AND ARTEFACT-STRIPPED SIDE BY SIDE. The artefact is near-constant in absolute terms - $0.57 sofar, $0.57 bare, $0.33 automemory - so what varies across arms is mostly the DENOMINATOR, which a percentage table hides; stripped, those three read about $5.26, $4.72 and $4.43. The operator's real question is not how big the tax is but whether the CONCLUSION MOVES when it is removed, and only the paired table answers that. If C1 and C4 survive stripping unchanged, Q3 is hygiene and $12 is cheap insurance; if either narrows or flips, the patch stops being a recommendation and becomes mandatory. ALSO ASKED: state the DIRECTION of bias per claim, unprompted. On C1 the tax falls harder on sofar than on automemory, so it biases AGAINST sofar and the current numbers understate our own case - the defensible direction to be wrong in. On C4 it runs the other way. On D19 it is not a direction but a family-sized gap, Cursor 0 against Codex 15. A skeptic who finds unaided that the bug flattered us discards the whole report; one handed where it did and did not has nothing left to find. COMPLEMENT ACCEPTED: DRIVE_VERIFY moves from bun to npm, profile untouched, with the frozen-footer reason stated."}
