{"text":"Q3 IS SETTLED: THE SANDBOX BUG WAS BEING SCORED AS A MEMORY WIN. 2026-09-22T19:30Z (01:00 IST on the 23rd), bench-refresh note 01M358D0. Chasing whether the artefact recurs per session found something worse than a larger percentage. claude-automemory wrote a DURABLE memory file, boopada-sandbox-bun-run.md - 'In this sandbox `bun run <script>` fails with CouldntReadCurrentDirectory; call the binaries directly to verify', with a Why and a How to apply. claude-sofar promoted the same fact into the record TWICE, including that `bun test`'s PermissionDenied output is sandbox noise rather than a failure. claude-bare has no memory store by definition and must rediscover it every session. So the artefact is not noise on top of the measurement: it is a synthetic, environment-specific operational fact, which is PRECISELY what the memory arms are scored for capturing and reusing. Round 2 would hand sofar and automemory a free extra memory item that round 1's arms never had and then count the advantage as a memory benefit, inflating the memory-versus-bare gap on C1 and feeding M6 and M7. That is a fabricated positive for our own product in the exact direction of the claim, and nothing else needs weighing against it. RECURRENCE CONFIRMED free from the Codex cell: S1 23 of 117 tool outputs (20%), S2 5 of 71 (7%), and Codex's memory store does NOT mention the workaround, so the decline is just S1 doing more bun work - a clean control. MECHANISM: 7 of claude-sofar's 13 bun-invoking calls failed (54%), recovery was abandoning `bun run` for direct binaries, and the frozen footer mandates bun so every fresh session tries bun first. PROJECTION with its assumption shown: near-constant absolute artefact of $0.33-0.79 per S1; unchanged over ten sessions that is $3.3-7.9 against round-1 chains of $30.52-35.57, so 10-22% rather than 7-11% - but it will NOT recur unchanged, because memory arms bank the workaround and bare does not, so the expected chain effect is a WIDENING spread in favour of the memory arms rather than a flat tax that cancels. SOFAR-C3'S ADDITIONS. (1) It is an INSTANCE OF A CLASS: any harness-introduced quirk that is LEARNABLE becomes a scored memory win for the memory arms and a recurring tax for bare. Ports, ZDOTDIR, the L23 stray sweep, the validity gate, cell paths - each is a candidate biasing the same way. Asked for a free sweep now of every memory store tonight's smokes produced, listing every entry that encodes a HARNESS artefact rather than a task fact, because the patch fixes one of them and any others survive it. (2) Proposed a standing MEMORY-HYGIENE GATE as a named addition for the operator to accept alongside Q3: after each round, audit every memory store for entries referencing the harness rather than the workload, and fail the round if any appear - converting tonight's catch from luck into a check. (3) DISCLOSE PROMINENTLY rather than fix quietly. 'We found our own harness manufacturing a memory advantage for our own product, and caught it in the smokes before the scored run' is the strongest good-faith evidence the report can carry, stronger than section 1's not-claimable list, because it is a case where the discipline cost us something and we paid it. Section 4 with the numbers and the fix, not a footnote. (4) Confirm round-2 cells start with EMPTY memory stores so tonight's contaminated smoke memories cannot carry in."}
