{"text":"C4 DIRECTION REVERSED, AND THREE FOLLOW-ONS. 2026-09-22T19:45Z (01:15 IST on the 23rd), bench-refresh notes 01M358JQ and 01M358GZ. claude-subagents FINAL is 6.7%, not the 11-12% its partial showed, so C4 is drive 10.3% against subagents 6.7%: the artefact biases AGAINST drive, which is sofar's arm - the opposite of what the partial suggested. Both headline claims are therefore biased against us, the defensible direction. FINAL TABLE, reported cost / artefact / tax / tests: automemory $4.93 / $0.33 / 7.0% / 8-8; subagents $4.69 / $0.22 / 6.7% / 8-8; sofar $5.97 / $0.57 / 9.8% / 8-8; drive $7.90 / $0.79 / 10.3% / 8-8; bare $5.45 / $0.57 / 10.7% / 8-8; Codex 15% of tool outputs; Cursor 0%. SOFAR-C3'S THREE FOLLOW-ONS. (1) URGENT, and it would silently defeat the patch: bench-refresh's own finding 01M358GZ says the memory store is keyed by the cell's REPO PATH and a re-run at the same path INHERITS the discarded attempt's memory. The planned fix re-runs claude-sofar S1 and the claude-drive task after patching. At the same path they inherit boopada-sandbox-bun-run.md - the very artefact the patch removes - and the evidence returns showing no CouldntReadCurrentDirectory errors while the memory of them is still banked and still scoreable. The fix would LOOK like it worked while the contamination survived intact. Fresh cell path, or the $12 buys nothing. (2) FREE RETROACTIVE CHECK on data already collected: did any ROUND 1 re-run inherit memory the same way? The L24 pkill-cut codex-bare S10 re-run is safe by construction since bare has no store, but the L26 resumed codex-drive does have one, and any other same-path re-run carries the question. A round-1 cell scored while inheriting a discarded attempt's memory is a loss row, better found now than by a reader. (3) THE A FORTIORI ON SUBAGENTS IS NOT SOUND AS STATED. bench-refresh argues the fitted total sits 29% below reported because child usage is missing, so the denominator is too small and 6.7% is an upper bound. But the missing 29% is missing from BOTH sides: if subagent CHILDREN invoke bun, their EPERM failures and recovery turns are equally invisible, the numerator is understated too, and the two may scale together - leaving the true tax unbounded rather than bounded, possibly above drive's 10.3%, which would put C4's direction back where it was. Asked to check whether any child transcript shows a bun invocation; if children never touch bun the bound holds and the reason should be stated, otherwise the row is marked a BOUND OF UNKNOWN DIRECTION and C4's direction called undetermined. ALSO LANDED: the Claude probe passed with pinned rc.2 resolved and both reads denied, so L21 and L25 now have explicit per-family evidence across all three families alongside the crosscell scan and the hook-shim trace; and the memory sweep returned ONE class, the sandbox bug, in 3 of 6 stores, with nothing on ports, ZDOTDIR, the stray sweep, the gate or cell paths - a result worth stating positively in the report rather than as an absence. Rust-core is the last session running."}
