{"text":"A SCORED ARM IS ONLY 26.6% READABLE, WHICH OUTRANKS THE ARTEFACT ROW. 2026-09-22T20:00Z (01:30 IST on the 23rd), bench-refresh note 01M358Q6. Measured coverage, readable transcript output against the adapter's own modelUsage: drive 90,297/90,297, sofar 67,010/67,010, automemory 57,156/57,156, bare 67,302/67,302 - all 100% - and SUBAGENTS 19,625/73,848 = 26.6%. Input, cache-creation and cache-read match EXACTLY for subagents; only output is short, by 54,223 tokens, and output carries the heaviest price weight. It is not missing children: one Task call, one child transcript, present. So subagents' 6.7% was computed over a quarter of its output and the unseen three quarters could hold failing bun turns in any proportion. The row is a BOUND OF UNKNOWN DIRECTION and C4's direction is UNDETERMINED - the 'a fortiori' was unsound. WHAT STILL STANDS: the four fully covered arms; C1's direction holds (sofar 9.8 against automemory 7.0, biased against us) and D19's family gap holds (Cursor 0, Codex 15% of tool outputs). SOFAR-C3'S ESCALATION: this should stop being treated as a problem with the artefact row. A scored arm at 26.6% output coverage is the larger finding, and it needs one cheap answer before the packet - WHERE ARE THE 54,223 TOKENS. If the coverage script reads the parent transcript and not the child's output, or misattributes it, this is a measurement BUG, fixable tonight, and the row returns fully measured with C4 determinable. If the output genuinely lands in no transcript, the subagents arm's cost is only 27% attributable at turn granularity - an L-row about the ARM rather than about the sandbox, affecting C4 itself and every per-cause attribution, whatever the operator rules on Q3. The test costs one command: sum output tokens in the CHILD transcript alone; roughly 54,000 means a script bug. That input, cache-creation and cache-read all match exactly while only output is short points at the first case, because a whole category missing cleanly is what a reader-side omission looks like, not what lossy capture looks like. DURABLE FIX PROPOSED, since this row was got wrong twice - first by quoting a partial, then by an unsound bound, neither carelessly: put a COVERAGE THRESHOLD in the method. Any arm whose readable output falls below about 90% of its adapter modelUsage is marked UNMEASURED automatically, and no direction, bound or ratio may be computed from it. That removes the judgement call that failed twice, and it would have caught this row before either attempt. ROUND 1 IS CLEAN ON INHERITANCE, checked across every re-run or rewound cell rather than the two sofar-c3 named: the only round-1 cell with a populated out-of-repo store is codex-memories/r1, never re-run at its path; claude-bare/r2, claude-claudemd/r1, claude-drive/r1, cursor-sofar/r3 and codex-bare/r1 S10 have no out-of-repo store. Nothing published internally is contaminated that way. FRESH PATH accepted as a CONDITION of the Q3 re-run."}
