NEVER been published, 404 at any version as drive-visibility confirmed while staging the rc, so the native core has never reached a user and this bug NEVER SHIPPED - an unshipped conformance bug found before publication is a success story, and the same sentence without the bound reads as a production defect. NAME THE REQUIREMENT: a last-bit difference in log changes a RANKING only where two BM25 scores sit within an ulp of each other, which is vanishingly rare; what it breaks is CONFORMANCE, where TypeScript and Rust must agree exactly. That is accurate and still sufficient reason to fix it, where calling it a ranking-quality bug would overstate it. bench-refresh's 2.11 mirror deliberately includes a case whose score sits right at a cutoff, which is exactly where this would have surfaced. The CI crosscheck is the durable part: a ported js_log pins us to fdlibm's stable algorithm and the crosscheck catches the day V8 changes underneath us."}
