n its own record. THE THIRD FINDING IS THE L11 SHAPE IN OUR OWN TOOLING: sofar_update_plan is a full replace that ALSO drops each phase's NOTE, because the note has no field in its schema. It preserved 4 phases and 14 tasks and silently lost the Phase 1 and Phase 2 summaries, restored with sofar_update_phase after diffing plan.md against a copy taken first. Directed to file it in PHASE-LIFECYCLE, which is open, owns sofar_update_phase, and whose surface phase notes are. Two things make it a FIX rather than another note: the workaround is ALREADY repo memory at .sofar/repo.md line 198 and an experienced session walked into it anyway, which is evidence that documentation is not the fix; and it is precisely the L11 loss shape - a write path silently discarding data because the field has no slot in the schema. The operator is being asked tonight whether L11 gets a new fix attempt, so these belong in front of them TOGETHER as one family rather than as two unrelated items."}
