es and retiring M2 would have taken that guidance with it. Naming the clause as superseded inside self-improve M8 and leaving M2 standing is correct when the unit of retirement is coarser than the unit of error. The clean fix is rust-core's: split M2 so the worktree guidance and the update_plan warning become separate memories. It also retired its OWN M7 from three hours earlier - 're-set the notes and diff' was a remembering, it failed within the same night, and it replaced rather than defended it. DECISION-GRADE DRIFT FOR THE OPERATOR'S Q2: Claude Code was 2.1.278 when the auto_mode steer was found a few hours ago and is 2.1.280 now - TWO releases inside one working night. That converts bench-refresh's L17 proposal from a reasonable accommodation into the only workable design, because a gate demanding an attachment-free session, or treating any version change as a re-run trigger, fires continuously against a binary moving twice a night. Recording the prompt hash and steer flags and re-running only when the STEER FLAGS change is what survives that cadence, and it is direct evidence that the frozen ~/.bench binary is what keeps the drift out of the measurement rather than a convenience. Directed to sofar-07 for the packet."}
